model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "xAI diagnostics retain only fixed monthly and weekly quota-field presence, null and numeric flags, the Home collector invocation time and closed claim, HTTP-start and completion-write states. A claim refusal never asserts a vendor call; a failed snapshot write never restamps the retained quota failure. Scheduled claim refusals do not erase completed probe evidence. Home keeps one metadata handoff per live credential before stdout, and the pool persists its closed projection independently of Home snapshots and process restarts. Pool reads retain their own request time and closed backoff, cap, admission and completion decision through the existing authenticated account and pool views. Older reads cannot replace newer evidence, and a delayed claimed reply cannot replace a completed state for the same Home attempt. Collection gates and authorization stay authoritative. No raw response, amount, product name, credential or token enters diagnostics, and no Home database model or version changes."
    }
  }
}
